My number is on the screen.
I go into the office.
An official is sitting at the desk.
I sit down on the chair.
"Good morning, Frau Flores," he says.
"Good morning," I say.
I give him my passport.
He checks the passport.
"You are Maya Flores from Mexico?" he asks.
"Yes, that is correct," I answer.
"And you are thirty-one years old?"
"Yes, I am thirty-one," I say.
"Do you have a flat here now?" he asks.
"Yes, I have a flat," I say.
He works on the computer for a moment.
"Do you already have a German telephone number?"
"No, I do not have a number yet," I answer.
"That is no problem," he says.
He stamps a paper.
"Here is your registration," he says.
He gives me the paper.
"Thank you very much," I say.
